{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten","id":991397,"title":"Why did Cappadocious allow himself to be eaten?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-22T08:05:30-07:00","id":991397,"title":"Why did Cappadocious allow himself to be eaten?","content":"As inspired by a recent trend where all the Diableries were, to borrow a phrase from another fictional universe &quot;just as planned&quot;. Tremere is Vampire Jesus, Tzitimze is Lugoj, Lasombra is in the Abyss, or something. But how does getting devoured (but apparently not fully, see the True Vessel) serve to push his plans forward?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:25:32-07:00","id":991402,"title":"","content":"There are a few reasons, the most reasonable being that he was utterly beyond sanity and believed that by freeing his soul he could then diablerise God.<br /> <br /> Another theory is that with Augustus being arguably the most accomplished Necromancer in such a short space of time (four centuries) Cappadocius wanted to inhabit the Giovanni, and have all that power at his fingertips.<br /> <br /> Yet another theory is that Cappadocius' soul was already split between multiple locations, and he wanted to pursue their reunification and ultimate ascension.<br /> <br /> None of the above seemed to go to plan for the silly old bastard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:58:30-07:00","id":991455,"title":"","content":"Because he had to die so the Giovanni Clan would exist in Modern Nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:48:01-07:00","id":991491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=991455#post991455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because he had to die so the Giovanni Clan would exist in Modern Nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metagamer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:49:02-07:00","id":991492,"title":"","content":"Cappadocious was already insane by the time of the rise of Christianity, like many of the Antediluvians and Methusalahs (immortality lies heavy on many minds), so you could give any reason, and it would likely be correct. For all we know, he was worried that his soul would be consumed by the light of the stars, and he thought that the only way to protect himself would be to wrap his soul with another soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:17:58-07:00","id":991716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=991492#post991492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all we know, he was worried that his soul would be consumed by the light of the stars, and he thought that the only way to protect himself would be to wrap his soul with another soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>That...was kind of erotic.<br /> <br /> I always thought soul eating could be romantic, but I never illustrated it so well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:40:55-07:00","id":991781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=991716#post991716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That...was kind of erotic.<br /> <br /> I always thought soul eating could be romantic, but I never illustrated it so well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god... Cappadocius X Augustus has to be a thing.<br /> <br /> RE &quot;deaths&quot; of Gen 3s, my personal approach is that while you can incapacitate a Gen 3, you can't utterly erase them from the universe. So Cappadocius still exists as a powerful Wraith and a portion of his Vitae still exists in both Augustus and the True Vessel. His return is possible. Set/Seth/Sutekh was killed and utterly destroyed by a pack of Garou, but his Soul is resting in Duat and the right sacrifice (say a massive pile of Gen 4 and 5 Brujah, which the Setites just happen to have canonically buried beneath the sands of Egypt) at the right time (say Gehenna) could bring him back from Duat with a new body... that's starving and goes forth to devour all of his Childer present. Tremere is trapped inside of Goratrix who is trapped inside of that mirror, Saulot is trapped inside of the Worm that used to be Tremere's body, either could be brought back properly with the right mystical mcguffin, or possibly by Gehenna. Lasombra exists within the Abyss, and Malkav is the Malkavian Madness Network. Why would they need bodies? They both presumably have Dominate 10, they have a huge number of bodies at their disposal. Ventru... come on? Seriously? Oh, yes, Troile killed Ventru. *Fortitude is a thing* *Dominate 3 is also a thing*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:50:27-07:00","id":991829,"title":"","content":"I do not mind the idea of an Antediluvian dying, but I think that a Clan always requires an existent 3rd generation to avoid becoming just a group of Bloodlines. While canon suggests that Set may be dead, what could Serpentis 10 do? Could it not potentially divide the soul among every mundane serpent in existence, allowing Set to observe the world until he/she/it decides to return? Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:26:40-07:00","id":991844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=991829#post991829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not mind the idea of an Antediluvian dying, but I think that a Clan always requires an existent 3rd generation to avoid becoming just a group of Bloodlines. While canon suggests that Set may be dead, what could Serpentis 10 do? Could it not potentially divide the soul among every mundane serpent in existence, allowing Set to observe the world until he/she/it decides to return? Just a thought...</div> </div> </div> </div>Serpentis 10, for me, is Flee Unto Duat. It allowed his Soul to rest there, utterly invulnerable, like an entombed Phaeroh, waiting for the right time to return. Like a perfect form of Torpor.<br /> <br /> Remember that Serpentis is only SNAKE POWERS up until level 4 really. From there and beyond there are some SNAKE POWERS but it's mostly Setist Symbolism, such as the ones that turn you into perfect warriors, or storms. So level 10 wouldn't necessarily have anything to do with Snakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:06:36-07:00","id":991914,"title":"","content":"As far as I recall It is never stated that Seth was utterly killed.<br /> <br /> Silente Strider's tribebook says he was vanquished and sealed, but I can't remember anything about him being destroyed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Silent Strider tribebook, page 18<br /> <br /> &quot;Shu-Horus severly injured Sutek, but rather than returning his blow, Sutekh went after Nephtys. He struck her down - as her magic had been depleted by empowering Shu-Horus - and then made her into a vampire. Shu-Horus managed to fight Sutekh almost to a standstill, and other Silent Striders sprung a trap, binding Suteh intro unconsciousness and imprisonment far underneath the earth.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-23-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:00:27-07:00","id":991934,"title":"","content":"A good point. The question then would be how long can the seal hold before Set is released?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:18:06-07:00","id":991941,"title":"","content":"You know for some strange reason it seems it's easier to bind or seal such entities rather than kill them.<br /> <br /> Seth is not the only Antediluvian who's got sealed, Troile is still sleeping in torpor under Carthage (the Romans cainite sealed him and Moloch with a Thaumaturgic ritual), Namtaru, if it is really an Antediluvian, is sealed too under Chorazin,when Tremere was expelled from his body he managed to trap saulot (albeit only for a brief time) by staking his body with a magic rod.<br /> <br /> And this is true even for other splats.<br /> Koschey and the Zmeis where too powerful to be killed, and it was easier to trap them, same goes for Kupala under the Carpatians, even Great Fenris, which is an Incarna has been shackled by Odin in some way with a powerful rite.<br /> <br /> <br /> With creatures of such power sealing seems a more useful (and effective) route.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:46:44-07:00","id":991961,"title":"","content":"Cappadocious wanted his physical body destroyed so that his spirit/soul could work full time on the non-material plane to enact whatever his plan was. He choose diablerie rather than another means because he was quite sure that if necessary he could &quot;return&quot; to physical reality by overpowering the psyche of the diablerist because his blood was in them.<br /> <br /> Of all the Antedeluvians, Cappadocious seemed to be the one who most had a plan of action (that the rest of us could see). His actions of the Feast of Folly, embrace of Augustus, letting him embrace his family, and all the weird things up to and after his embrace indicated there was some master plan in place. Whatever the plan was, it involved making sure that he culled all the ones who disappointed him and saved the ones he wanted that would prove useful in Gehenna.<br /> <br /> I assumed that his plan involved coming back to earth, wiping out the Giovanni except for a few individuals who secretly served him, and bringing back all the odd ball Cappadocians he had made sure were preserved. Of all the clans in Vampire, I always thought the Giovanni were the ones most obviously doomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:29:41-07:00","id":992014,"title":"","content":"I think Tzimisce is the greatest mastermind of all: the whole Anarch Revolt was just his doing to achieve a masterstroke in the Jyhad, &quot;helping&quot; the anarchs through his child Lambach, giving the young Tzimisces the means to free themselves from the shackles of their elders and bound them all at the same time (ahahahaha Sauron, watch and learn!), ensuring the spread of his blood among the whole Sabbat, getting far from the Old World and taking New York undercity as his personal nest while completing the ascension to Azhi Dahaka.<br /> <br /> Saulot too is quite the gamer, his only error was not taking in account the fact that a mage as powerful as Tremere would have been able to resist his mental powers, locking him in a 800 years psychic battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if the theory &quot;Ravnos is Ravana&quot; is correct than also the Ravnos Antediluvian would be a great planner: forcing the Technocracy to use nuclear weapons so he could muster tainted souls for his ascension to Demon Emperor.<br /> <br /> The only Antediluvians who don't seem to have &quot;a plan&quot; are Toreador and Ennoia, or at least if they have we know nothing about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 10-23-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:49:17-07:00","id":992474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=992014#post992014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Tzimisce is the greatest mastermind of all: the whole Anarch Revolt was just his doing to achieve a masterstroke in the Jyhad, &quot;helping&quot; the anarchs through his child Lambach, giving the young Tzimisces the means to free themselves from the shackles of their elders and bound them all at the same time (ahahahaha Sauron, watch and learn!), ensuring the spread of his blood among the whole Sabbat, getting far from the Old World and taking New York undercity as his personal nest while completing the ascension to Azhi Dahaka.<br /> <br /> Saulot too is quite the gamer, his only error was not taking in account the fact that a mage as powerful as Tremere would have been able to resist his mental powers, locking him in a 800 years psychic battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if the theory &quot;Ravnos is Ravana&quot; is correct than also the Ravnos Antediluvian would be a great planner: forcing the Technocracy to use nuclear weapons so he could muster tainted souls for his ascension to Demon Emperor.<br /> <br /> The only Antediluvians who don't seem to have &quot;a plan&quot; are Toreador and Ennoia, or at least if they have we know nothing about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd always assumed Saolut's reasons were more to do with Tzimisce than the upstart mage. Remember, Garotrix and Etrius are both reputed to be better sorcerers than Tremere and clan Tremere ALL have Tzimisce blood in them, (something that serves to ruin Tremre's plans in one Gehenna scenario). Myself and other players I spoke to always assumed Saolut let himself get taken to develop a cure for the taint of the Tzimisce eldest. After all, numerous accounts suggest Samael was the first to try to kill Tzimisce. It's likely that after that failed (due to Tzimisce's literal rebirth) Saolut recognised the danger they were in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-25-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:13:15-07:00","id":992521,"title":"","content":"Of course, a relevant question may be whether Tzimisce has spiritually contaminated Saulot. I am curious, do you think that Saulot could survive if someone diablerized his current body or would the trauma of a second diablerie be too severe even for an Antediluvian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:41:53-07:00","id":992536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=991716#post991716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That...was kind of erotic.<br /> <br /> I always thought soul eating could be romantic, but I never illustrated it so well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assimilating a person's entire being with that of your own?<br /> <br /> How could that be romantic? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:41:04-07:00","id":992577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh god... Cappadocius X Augustus has to be a thing. </div> </div> </div>So their couples name would be &quot;Cappagustus&quot;? Or.... OMG OMG OMG<br /> <br /> &quot;Audacious&quot;!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","user":"Nosimplehiway","date":". 10-24-2016, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:51:46-07:00","id":992602,"title":"","content":"He didn't allow it. He demanded it.<br /> <br /> My theory on Cappadocious goes something like this:<br /> <br /> Cappy had a clan, obsessed with dead stuff and mold and graves and such. Mostly pretty literal in their thinking. Maybe one of their main duties in Enoch was clearing out the dead bodies, and they grew to like their work a little too much. They were gravediggers, morticians, funeral pyre builders, the guys who drag around a wagon calling &quot;bring out your dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> Cappy set his sights higher. He wanted to really understand death. To grok it. So, he began embracing folks who had some real insight, at least for the times. Professional mourners, morticians, probably some mummifiers (is that the word?), priests of death gods and psychopomps, etc. Thinkers and mystics, rather than simple disposal technicians.<br /> <br /> But, he still had all these, well let's call them what they were, illiterate death fetishists and random hangers-on filling his payroll. So, he had the Feast of Folly to clean house. He found the low class grave diggers obsolete and so just... disposed of them. Cold. Out with the old clan, in with the new.<br /> <br /> Now, that seemed promising for a time, if unfocused. Then he met the priests of a certain religion whose deity (some guy named Yahweh, from some crappy backwater in the Levant), incarnated, died and returned from the dead, then went to the Other Side again. Oh, and His religion used blood to ritually transfer his divine emanations. Cappy figured he hit the motherlode. God or no god, if he came to earth as a human, he had a human soul. That means when he dies, he creates a wraith. If his followers believe in the power of His blood, then in the spirit world, that should be a way of siphoning his power. And, that is something, with the right disciplines, a 3rd gen can eat!<br /> <br /> But, how? He needed somebody better at dealing with the other side of the shroud than he was. I mean, when it came to animating corpses, controlling dead bodies through their blood, and spreading rotty stinky diseases, Cappy was the best of the best. But, on the other side of the Shroud? And going there to make wraiths not just do what you want, but think you are worshiping them in the process? He was a rank amateur. But, hey isn't that what Italian ancestor worship is all about! Hey, those guys up in the swamps of the Northern Adriatic seem pretty good at that stuff.<br /> <br /> So, he embraced Augie. But... the problem was the Giovanni were no one's tool. So, Cap needed a few things. He needed to clean out the losers on his payroll; Mortis was old hat. He also needed to establish a power base to fund his research. Oh, and he needed a more tractable clan. This business of Japheth and Lazarus and those losers having to be asked nicely every time Cap wanted them to do something small (like slaughtering the old clan, for example) was just... frustrating.<br /> <br /> Cappy already had high levels of Fortitude and Mortis. He just needed to learn some Dominate, which he did. Keeping in mind how Dominate lets you possess people, Fortitude keeps you whole and intact; and Mortis lets you think of the rules of physical life and death as vague suggestions... how powerful of a combo discipline would you need to create a failsafe where anyone who diablerizes you gets possessed instead. Permanently. Not a rhetorical question. Dominate 7, Fortitude 8, Mortis 8, maybe? Maybe with Auspex, which Cappy had, thrown in to cinch the psychic contest? It would take a century (or three) to design and learn, but, hey, Cap's not in a hurry.<br /> <br /> Poor old Uncle Augie was drinking from a firehose and got drowned. Kaput. Out like a light. And Cap had no doubt at all what the outcome would be. Cap was now not only in Augie's body, he had a sympathetic blood connection to every single dead body with blood related to Augie. Yep, he has a direct sympathetic connection to the entire clan, through which to use his Dominate and Auspex. The other Antes with that combo are Malkav and Tzimisce; think of the highly networked, non-focal existence they built in their bloodlines.<br /> <br /> That's the Giovanni today. An entire clan (and family) of blood puppets to an antedeluvian they thought they destroyed centuries ago. He's just more subtle than Malkv or Tzimisce. He doesn't feel the need for their attention seeking behavior.<br /> <br /> Clan Giovanni built a powerbase, worked to tear down the shroud, researched Necromancy and rituals that will empower them on the Other Side, and maintained a presence in the church of that blood-death god that piqued Cap's interest. They were even nice enough to take out the garbage, which was his old, now obsolete, clan. They did everything he needed to prepare to diablerize a god.<br /> <br /> Oh, and while most folks think he's insane for wanting to diablerize God, let's remember Cappadocius &quot;knew him when&quot;. Back in the day, on the old block, Yahweh was just one of many in a pantheon of Semitic tribal spirits who managed to build up a following in the Neolithic Levant, roughly equal in power to, say, Set or a maybe a second gen. Cappadocius believes (and in the WoD cosmology might even be right) that Yahweh managed to leverage sleeper belief to catapult Himself into the top spot in the spirit world during the Age of Faith. But the Renaissance, Enlightenment and the 20th century knocked him down a few pegs, mojo-wise. Most sleepers either don't really <i>believe </i>in Him or see Him as Morgan Freeman in a white suit. Yahweh is slipping from lack of belief, and soon, maybe, will be vulnerable. Then Cappadocius will feed on the divine soul of Yahweh, Himself.<br /> <br /> And both Clan and Family Giovanni are built to help him do just that.<br /> <br /> Every few months someone on the boards posts a topic asking what theme songs apply to the WoD. My nomination for Cappadocius:<br /> <br /> &quot;He was born on a Christmas Day, when the New York Times said God is dead and the war's begun...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:52:52-07:00","id":992991,"title":"","content":"I've always been torn on Cappadocius. On the one hand it seems preposterous that an upstart like Augustus could consume arguably the most mystically accomplished Antediluvian. On the other hand I also kind of hate the meme that the Antediluvians are impossible to defeat to destroy no matter what you do. The possibility ought to exist that Cappadocius just done fucked up. <br /> <br /> I split the difference. In my own canon Cappadocius foresaw the Giovanni's treachery and rather than quash it chose to try and turn it to his advantage, using the Usurpation as a new Feast of Folly (he never seems to have liked his own clan all that much) and using Giovanni's diablerie of him as a sacrifice in a terrifying ritual that would allow him to achieve even greater power. Except something went wrong. He missed something. Augustus consumed him and the Usurpation purged his clan almost completely. Some say his soul is still out there somewhere. Not a Wraith, not a Vampire, not a Spirit, but something <i>else</i>. How could this be if Augustus is indeed now of the third generation? That is something truly known only to the most ancient necromancers. <br /> <br /> What to me stands in for the Giovanni's &quot;Antediluvian dread&quot; is the Premascines. They isolate themselves from the rest of the family and nearly all interactions with them turn hostile if prolonged. Why then does Augustus allow them to be venerated? Why the pomp and offerings? Why are not those family members with the Sanguine Incongruity destroyed as abominations? Because Augustus is <i>afraid</i>. He could take one or two of the Premascines on his own no problem, but he's isn't sure that on his best night all the Premascines couldn't roll up on him together and murder him if the spirit suddenly took them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:32:14-07:00","id":993075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand I also kind of hate the meme that the Antediluvians are impossible to defeat to destroy no matter what you do. </div> </div> </div>I agree that antedeluvians aren't impossible to destroy or that every time one of them is diablerized it must go bad. (I think the True Brujah are so cranky because Troile did it right. I also have my suspicions about the sudden change in Set's religion and public persona around 500 bce.) But, in Cappadocius' case, given that he is the antedeluvian of a clan associated with death and endings, it seems he could manipulate the system if he needed to. If any of the antedeluvians should have power over their own life and death, it's him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:31:19-07:00","id":993103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=992602#post992602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, he still had all these, well let's call them what they were, illiterate death fetishists and random hangers-on filling his payroll. So, he had the Feast of Folly to clean house. He found the low class grave diggers obsolete and so just... disposed of them. Cold. Out with the old clan, in with the new.<br /> <br /> Now, that seemed promising for a time, if unfocused. Then he met the priests of a certain religion whose deity (some guy named Yahweh, from some crappy backwater in the Levant), incarnated, died and returned from the dead, then went to the Other Side again. Oh, and His religion used blood to ritually transfer his divine emanations. Cappy figured he hit the motherlode. God or no god, if he came to earth as a human, he had a human soul. That means when he dies, he creates a wraith. If his followers believe in the power of His blood, then in the spirit world, that should be a way of siphoning his power. And, that is something, with the right disciplines, a 3rd gen can eat!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm pretty sure the Feast of Folly happened after Cappadocius (or even the Cappadocian) embraced christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:20:25-07:00","id":993160,"title":"","content":"I go with something more exotic that Cappadocius DID diablerize God.<br /> <br /> Just not the Christian one.<br /> <br /> Or maybe he did and it was *A* Christian one.<br /> <br /> Now he's a Neverborn in the Underworld, ruling over a Heaven of his own choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-09-2019, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:13:03-07:00","id":993182,"title":"","content":"I acutally ran an entire Orpheus campaign based around the notion that Cappadocious had succeeded in diablerising the Elohim. Things had gone well for him at first but within years the power started to eat him from the inside out because it was too much for him to control. Although all other vampire clans were wiped out come 50 years of Godhood he simply expired and the power remained as a burning, untapped ball of burning white potential in the spirit world. Anyone who tried to control or absorb it was destroyed utterly by it in seconds or less. From then on the power of God was controlled by nobody, could be controlled by nobody, and the universe started to die.<br /> <br /> I started the players thinking they were in a perfectly normal modern day setting and then occasionally fed them little cards with answers to questions that would come up later. 'When did World War 2 end?' turned out to be '1962 with the dropping of a nuclear bomb on Berlin'. Add to that the cold war was still going on in 2013 and various other enticing 'this world is noticeably worse' pieces of trivia. By the time the game began the spirit world and real world were getting closer because the entire world was circling the drain and about to be subsumed by another reality. In essence one universe (my take on the mysterious known in-game as 'grandmother') was consuming another, and everyone would be lost to the worse-than-hell non-existence of being diablerised. There was no way to reverse the process and the campaign just got bleaker and bleaker as they tried and failed to restore any hope.<br /> <br /> I never really gave the players, (all humans that could step in to the spirit realm) a solution to the problem, the end was the end, but they found an interesting half-victory. The final Cappadocians left were busy escaping to the new universe that was consuming their own dying one, (to a universe in which Cappy failed) and showed the players the way, but to pass through a person needed to be undead, and to have undergone a transition to escape the spectral hive mind and regain their humanity. They needed to become what was known in Orpheus canon as an 'Orphan-Grinder'.In an unexpected final move a PC, a young Hindi physicist named Devi Nagra (who had been through the worst of it all including learning that her faith was, apparently, false) absorbed what was left of the power of the Elohim and used her last thought before being obliterated utterly to kill the entire world and force them through the harrowing transition. Being a spectre in an alien reality, she reasoned, was better than being compressed in to nothingness.<br /> <br /> As the storyteller, I was floored by this move.<br /> <br /> Her moment of godhood lasted less than a second before her body and soul were destroyed utterly by the untamed power but she saved potential billions from a fate worse than hell in doing so. As the previously living found themselves flushed in to the spirit world the first thing they saw was the burning white figure of Devi as Kali the Destroyer pointing their way to the new world.<br /> <br /> The moment was so palpable and poignant that, I kid you not, two of the players were actually crying.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the typical canonical approach is that both Cappadocious and Augustus failed. Cappadocious' soul escaped diablerie, (as is laid out explicitly in the Giovanni chronlices) and most of what was left, (though not all of him) was destroyed in the 6th maelstrom. I like this solution best because it both avoids the 'you can't ever beat an antediluvian' trope but also shows that Augustus wasn't up to the task. It also puts an interesting spin on the Giovanni - that Uncle Auggie has to play the part of a 3rd generation vampire but simply lacks that kind of power and so his bluff has been getting thinner and thinner over the centuries. That by modern nights his own clan is starting to suspect he is weak and desperate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-26-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:25:37-07:00","id":993213,"title":"","content":"And those moments are why we play. Brava.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:38:16-07:00","id":993220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=992991#post992991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been torn on Cappadocius. On the one hand it seems preposterous that an upstart like Augustus could consume arguably the most mystically accomplished Antediluvian. On the other hand I also kind of hate the meme that the Antediluvians are impossible to defeat to destroy no matter what you do. The possibility ought to exist that Cappadocius just done fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go read the NPC section in the Giovanni Saga/Chronicles, Cappadocius' verbatim stats are: &quot;To provide Traits for Cappadocius would be ridiculous. No one in this story could affect him without his permission.&quot;<br /> <br /> Canonically, the diablerie happened solely because Cappadocius wanted it to happen and allowed it to, and for no other reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5853-krb","name":"KRB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:14:50-07:00","id":993391,"title":"","content":"I prefer the idea that Augustus didn't diablerize Cappadocius at all. And that the purge of the old clan didn't happen as such, they just sort of waned while the Giovanni waxed.<br /> <br /> Way I see it, Augustus probably wanted to diablerize old Cappy, and took steps towards that goal. He had his more loyal childer take gangs to strike out at the other fourth gen Cappadocians, eliminating his competition in one fell swoop. Some perished, others survived by going into hiding. At the same time, Auggy came to Cappadocius, seeking to eat him.<br /> <br /> As he was in position to do the deed, Cappadocius woke up and smiled at him. He said, &quot;Augustus, I already know you planned to devour me, body, mind, and soul. I also know you seek to gain control of the Clan for yourself.&quot; He then rose to his feet, patted Augustus on the shoulder, and took off a piece of clothing that Clan Cappadocius identified their founder by (a scarf or amulet or something). &quot;While I'd hate to disappoint you, lad,&quot; Cappadocius said, &quot;take consolation in knowing that one of those things will happen tonight.&quot;<br /> <br /> He then handed the piece to Augustus, and walked away, never to be seen again. Auggy, absolutely terrified at this moment, could do nothing but stand frozen on the spot for a minute. Then, regaining his composure, he donned the item, walked out, and began telling everyone that he totally diablerized Cappadocius, and had all the powers of an Antedeluvian. Any of the old clan who protested this usurpation were hunted down, while the rest of the Cappadocians decided it was easier to keep their heads down. The Ventrue and Giovanni had their war for a while, and then have their peace agreement.<br /> <br /> And from there, the Giovanni simply out-bred their Cappadocian cousins. This being because the Cappadocians, ever since the Feast of Folly, were deathly afraid of inviting their founder's ire by embracing too wildly. No one wanted to start a new Feast, so they took childer sparingly. Even after Augustus claimed to have diablerized Cappadocius, not all of the Clan necessarily believed Cappadocius was actually gone. Either because Augustus was lying, or because the diablerie wasn't the end of old Cappy. So even after Augustus's ascension to head of &quot;Clan&quot; Giovanni, the old guard decided it wasn't worth taking chances.<br /> <br /> Centuries of time, accident, the Anarch Revolt, and simple attrition wore down the numbers of the Cappadocians, until they were little more than a bloodline. Meanwhile, the Giovanni took childer freely from their mortal family, and proceeded to amass a great deal of temporal and supernatural power. Some Elders of other Clans remember the days when the Cappadocians were not just a Clan, but a High Clan (at least in most parts of Europe). But most of the younger generations have never heard of the gravediggers, let alone seen one. Only a few Camarilla domains have Cappadocians in them - insular and paranoid broods whose antipathy towards the Giovanni upstarts is outweighed by their paranoia of old Cappy. Meanwhile, the Sabbat has a slowly building Cappadocian Antitribu population, who understandably take a militant attitude towards Cappadocius and his fellow Antedeluvians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-26-2016, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T04:29:43-07:00","id":993425,"title":"","content":"I think it's fair to say that as Augustus never Embraced after the diablerie, we've no way of knowing whether he made it to 3rd Gen. I would say he didn't, due to the incomplete nature of the diablerie, but kept this fact hidden. It's not like people go around with Generation signs flashing above their heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:32:01-07:00","id":993535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=993425#post993425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not like people go around with Generation signs flashing above their heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth. Over the years I've grown into more and more of a fan of the idea that the Kindred conception of Generation is nowhere near as neat as its presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T18:40:33-07:00","id":994317,"title":"","content":"According to the Giovanni Chronicles, Old Cappa not only knew Augustus was planning on Diablerie but that was part of his plan. The stuff he talks about when the PCs meet him in Giovanni Chronicles I, he comes across crazy, likely with a Messiah Complex. The whole thing comes across as him trying to create his version of the Crucifixion, with him as Christ and Augustus as Judas. And there's the implication that it was what he had planned from as far back as when he brought the Giovani into the Clan which sucks for his poor childer. <br /> <br /> But then it's pretty clear that the entire Third Generation is made up of self-centered assholes, inhuman monsters, batshit insane lunatics or some combination thereof so it's not really surprising that Cappadocius is a self-centered asshole and a batshit insane lunatic. Though it kind of does make him worse than Augustus. He's just a self-centered asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:09:09-07:00","id":994500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=994317#post994317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Giovanni Chronicles, Old Cappa not only knew Augustus was planning on Diablerie but that was part of his plan. The stuff he talks about when the PCs meet him in Giovanni Chronicles I, he comes across crazy, likely with a Messiah Complex. The whole thing comes across as him trying to create his version of the Crucifixion, with him as Christ and Augustus as Judas. And there's the implication that it was what he had planned from as far back as when he brought the Giovani into the Clan which sucks for his poor childer.<br /> <br /> But then it's pretty clear that the entire Third Generation is made up of self-centered assholes, inhuman monsters, batshit insane lunatics or some combination thereof so it's not really surprising that Cappadocius is a self-centered asshole and a batshit insane lunatic. Though it kind of does make him worse than Augustus. He's just a self-centered asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div>More precisely, they want the same things player-characters want, just on a more ambitious scale: to transcend/escape the vampiric condition via Golconda or some other method, to become the most powerful vampire ever, to become the rulers of everything, and to gain petty revenge/adoration/various soap-opera childishness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:21:17-07:00","id":994507,"title":"","content":"Strange, the people I have played with have never wanted to transcend the vampire condition but, instead, to maintain their humanity while being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:32:47-07:00","id":995152,"title":"","content":"I did give more than one example of the things player-characters tend to want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T09:07:39-07:00","id":1482376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=992991#post992991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the one hand it seems preposterous that an upstart like Augustus could consume arguably the most mystically accomplished Antediluvian. On the other hand I also kind of hate the meme that the Antediluvians are impossible to defeat to destroy no matter what you do. The possibility ought to exist that Cappadocius just done fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm relatively new to the WoD in general and VtM in particular, but I agree.<br /> If the 3rd gens are basically deus ex machina from final death, even by their oldest childer, how did they manage to kill their own, presumably equally more powerful, sires?<br /> <br /> Like sure, it's possible Capp knew what was gonna happen and had his horcrux's ready to go. But I like the idea that he miscalculated something and ended up screwing Giovanni's efforts to jump up a generation, and sent himself to the Underworld instead of to heaven for his godly snack attack.<br /> I can't find the reference again, but I read somewhere that someone in the WoD canon managed to glimpse heaven and it was just a white void, no god, no heavenly host, no paradise etc. So heck maybe letting A.G. suck him down worked perfectly, and Capp drank all the Holy Kool-aid he could get his dead undead fangs into, but he just couldn't handle the raw power of G-Diddy's juice and it blasted him down to the underworld as a wraith and left heaven an empty shell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27434-uncletroll","user":"UncleTroll","date":". 05-30-2022, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27434-uncletroll","name":"UncleTroll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T11:22:03-07:00","id":1482386,"title":"","content":"Kind of fitting that a dead thread about Cappadocius is resurrected with necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T12:44:58-07:00","id":1482395,"title":"","content":"I'd close it but am inclined to give it a benny due to actually being on topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T18:25:16-07:00","id":1482431,"title":"","content":"Cappadocious was insane. He was so insane the amount of marauders and Malkavians decreased because he was hogging the otherwise freely available around of crazy flowing through the universe.<br /> <br /> Joking side, Cappadocious was making irrational decisions by the time he planned for the embrace of the Giovanni, and this did not get better as time went on. I also suspect he was manipulated by outside forces, which exploited his weaknesses.<br /> <br /> I have a personal theory about all of that as well. According to the lore, Cappadocious went into the underworld when he was embraced and lost part of himself in the process. He was always trying to recover this lost part of himself and the experience helps explain why he became obsessed with death, ghosts, and the underworld. My theory is what he lost was his Shadow, or an aspect of his darker self. All wraiths possess a shadow, which try to manipulate them into self destruction. I think Cappadocious lost shadow became Dis Pater, or the mysterious patron of the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Edit To Add: The Giovanni supposedly had a plan called &quot;Endless Night.&quot; This was almost certainty something they inherited from the original Cappadocians and their founder in particular. This plan involved the destruction of the barrier between the worlds of the living and the worlds of the dead. Letting himself be (mostly) diablerized was a step in this master plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-30-2022, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T19:35:20-07:00","id":1482438,"title":"","content":"In Giovanni Chronicles it turns out that Cappadocious ended up falling to his Shadow and became a crazy revenge obsessed Spectre. Ultimately Cappadocious was a bumblefuck who didn't know nearly as much as he thought he did. It seems like he thought he'd go to heaven when he died and then he'd be able to diablarize God but then, oops, he didn't go to heaven. Because he wasn't nearly as &quot;good&quot; of a person as he thought he was. Which is pretty genre appropriate since there are a lot of assholes out there who are absolutely, positively, confident that they will go to heaven when they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:04:28-07:00","id":1482442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482438#post1482438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Giovanni Chronicles it turns out that Cappadocious ended up falling to his Shadow and became a crazy revenge obsessed Spectre. Ultimately Cappadocious was a bumblefuck who didn't know nearly as much as he thought he did. It seems like he thought he'd go to heaven when he died and then he'd be able to diablarize God but then, oops, he didn't go to heaven. Because he wasn't nearly as &quot;good&quot; of a person as he thought he was. Which is pretty genre appropriate since there are a lot of assholes out there who are absolutely, positively, confident that they will go to heaven when they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Vampires go he was an ok person, and it isn't impossible that he was good enough to go to Heaven, depending on how you define this.<br /> <br /> But the whole idea of Diablerizing God was plain stupid from the get go, and the time dedicated to it probably didn't helped a lot. With this, his mystical workings probably had a dozen flaws due to wrong premises and then he sent himself to what was actually the only place he could send himself. Maybe he tried to hit a non-existent or Truly closed place, or just should have to turn left at Albuquerque. Either way he just plain failed and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T20:18:30-07:00","id":1482445,"title":"","content":"Personally, I much prefer an interpretation where everything goes according to Cappadocius\u2019 plan rather than him being a crazy fool who screwed up. Perhaps the Feast of Folly was not to eliminate the Cappadocians who weren\u2019t Christians or scholars, but rather Cappadocius was eliminating the weaklings who spend all of their time with their noses in books rather than truly studying death. It was those who survived being entombed who ultimately survived the purge by the Giovanni, aside from a few individuals. Part of the Cappadocians were killed by the Feast of Folly. Part of the Clan were destroyed in the Giovanni usurpation. Many of the Giovanni were eliminated with the creation of the Hecata. Perhaps this was Cappadocius\u2019 original goal, which he foresaw millennia ago.<br /> <br /> It could be that Giovanni never diablerized him, it was just a trick. Perhaps more interesting is that Cappadocius still secretly rules has Clan is a different form. Just as some of the Antediluvians have ascended to being not quite vampire anymore - Lasombra, Gangrel, Tzimisce - Cappadocius could be a spectral creature more powerful than ever before.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing is more interesting to me than him being the only Antediluvian to really get diablerized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T21:19:28-07:00","id":1482458,"title":"","content":"Would be funny if it turned out he succeeded in eating God, but then discovered that the nature of omniscience leads to infinite apathy, resulting in a deist God who just lets the universe spin. He ate the apathetic, deist God and then became an apathetic, deist God. His victory had absolutely no effect on anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T23:21:56-07:00","id":1482465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482458#post1482458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be funny if it turned out he succeeded in eating God, but then discovered that the nature of omniscience leads to infinite apathy, resulting in a deist God who just lets the universe spin. He ate the apathetic, deist God and then became an apathetic, deist God. His victory had absolutely no effect on anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every vampire that's ever died has diablerized god upon meeting them. Each becoming the next incarnation of god, and each incarnation cares just as little as the last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27434-uncletroll","name":"UncleTroll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:07:46-07:00","id":1482472,"title":"","content":"Not fond of Cappadocious on account of us knowing way too much about him. I do have an idea that Cappadocius and Augustus were the two most recent hosts of the soul of the Cappadocian/Giovanni/Hecata ante in clan history. Alternatively he was never the real founder, but a figure head and the actual Antediluvian is working offscreen. Perhaps one of its identities is &quot;Dis Pater&quot; the mysterious wraithly benefactor of the Giovanni. Or their founder really is just a pile of ashes, any of it works for me.<br /> <br /> As for why... I don't imagine this was originally why, because V5's metaplot hadn't even been conceived back then as far as I know, but as of now I'd imagine it was done with the formation of the Hecata in mind. The rise of the Giovanni was important for that. Using successive and careful purges to divide a bunch of aimless, layabout nerds into three bloodlines (loyal to their founders and so conveniently guided by a mysterious ancient) and then converging those bloodlines together into an obscenely rich global apocalypse cult with mastery over life, death and undeath and a stranglehold on vampiric necromancy.<br /> <br /> What step the Hecata is in the plan is unknown, but so far &quot;poison the universe and watch it die&quot; appears to be on the to do list. Perhaps Cappadocius' plan was to kill god, scrap the universe he built and then build his own universe and rule over that as god. Maybe he thinks by destroying the universe, he'll be able to expose god/the soul of the universe and diablerise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-31-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T05:33:14-07:00","id":1482482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482445#post1482445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I much prefer an interpretation where everything goes according to Cappadocius\u2019 plan rather than him being a crazy fool who screwed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole problem with his plan in this regard is if you accept his goal to Diablerize God, that is relatively core to his description and development. Cappadocius is one of the Antes that is best defined as character, and he is, indeed, an interesting character. So there's a trade-off to this, but it can surely be done with more or less sacrifice of this character.<br /> <br /> Most people won't take this plan seriously. By myself I find plots at this scale ridiculous and boring, but I also prefer a more mundane destiny to <b>all</b> Antes in my games, so it's a matter of personal preference. If it works for your game, you can take everything at face value on that. If you scrap it as the real plan, then you must define, or at least have a rough idea, of what the real plan could be.<br /> <br /> But even going by the route of Cappadocius being a &quot;crazy fool&quot;, it doesn't mean that he ended up being truly Diablerized. He can have any destiny you want to give him, he was still immensely powerful and knowledgeable. Maybe what happened was according to plan regardless of the foolishness of his end goal because it wasn't the plan's finale yet. Maybe it failed, but the Ante survived and then just recouped his losses. Maybe he got Diablerized, but isn't the only one that ended up that way or worse.<br /> <br /> It isn't even the worst blunder people ascribe to an Ante. While it is possible that Lasombra ascended, actually a lot of people think he probably just managed to snuff himself out of existence like an idiot, trying to gobble up something less abstract and more obviously dangerous than God. Or even that it was a no-win situation, the so-called &quot;Ego-Death&quot; where success would make him so diffused in his new state as to be effectively dead as a person, becoming indistinguishable from what the Abyss was before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T18:29:02-07:00","id":1482559,"title":"","content":"About the Tremere and their giant worm Antideluvian, has the worm been confirmed destroyed by the Inquisition? Has anything about it's fate been confirmed at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T19:53:54-07:00","id":1482566,"title":"","content":"Part of me is inclined to jump on the 'Cappadocious is insane' bandwagon, but I'm also reminded of ToJ Gehenna and how it reinforced all the different ways in which Antediluvians simply changed into things much more than bloodsucking vampires. Ante's by definition play by a different set of rules and are supposed to represent truly alien, unknowable minds so it's really hard to justify appending 'human' labels like sanity or insanity. I mean in a way I could see why he might think it would work - spirits devouring other spirits to grow more powerful isn't exactly an unsuual thing in WoD as a rule from what I recall, and if he can gain enough power he might be able to assimilate a deity. I mean we saw something similar proposed with Voormas in ToJ:Ascension, and Revelations of the Dark Mother suggested the masculine 'God' may not have actually been the creator-entity (in that sense it would be analogous to Cappadocious trying to consume Lucifer. And if you accept the premise of the Ante being insane how would he know the difference between an Elohim and a true deity?) <br /> <br /> Really how you try to explain it will depend greatly on how you piece together the cosmology and what assumptions you're willing or unwilling to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:11:17-07:00","id":1482632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482559#post1482559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Tremere and their giant worm Antideluvian, has the worm been confirmed destroyed by the Inquisition? Has anything about it's fate been confirmed at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was &quot;just&quot; Saulot and he's free as a bird.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;White Worm&quot; thing was just a weird secret society in Clan Tremere the Authors put there to make gonzo crossover with WtA and throw in Lovecraftian themes and references, extremely on the nose ones. They're based in a &quot;mysterious book&quot; that simply describes the Umbra from a Black Spiral Dancer POV, with an author that is exactly the same of the Necronomicon in the Lovecraftian Mythos, but plays no other part in the setting never again, and the order simply concluded they have to pledge themselves to the Wyrm and shifted their worries from the Gehenna to the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the &quot;White Worm&quot; was reused here and there as a name for Saulot, directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  typo 06-01-2022, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:36:19-07:00","id":1482639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482566#post1482566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me is inclined to jump on the 'Cappadocious is insane' bandwagon, but I'm also reminded of ToJ Gehenna and how it reinforced all the different ways in which Antediluvians simply changed into things much more than bloodsucking vampires. Ante's by definition play by a different set of rules and are supposed to represent truly alien, unknowable minds so it's really hard to justify appending 'human' labels like sanity or insanity. I mean in a way I could see why he might think it would work - spirits devouring other spirits to grow more powerful isn't exactly an unsuual thing in WoD as a rule from what I recall, and if he can gain enough power he might be able to assimilate a deity. I mean we saw something similar proposed with Voormas in ToJ:Ascension, and Revelations of the Dark Mother suggested the masculine 'God' may not have actually been the creator-entity (in that sense it would be analogous to Cappadocious trying to consume Lucifer. And if you accept the premise of the Ante being insane how would he know the difference between an Elohim and a true deity?)<br /> <br /> Really how you try to explain it will depend greatly on how you piece together the cosmology and what assumptions you're willing or unwilling to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes a lot more sense actually than just stating &quot;he's just stupid insane&quot;, even though the being likely has all mental traits at 10 lol. I think a gehenna plot like the one with Voormas, but featuring Cappadocious could be very interesting. I mean, what if he succeeded? Really, anything is in the ST hands. This is the great part of WoD. There are so many plots to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:25:09-07:00","id":1482671,"title":"","content":"I think that Cappadocius makes for a very interesting Ante, because he mixes so many actions that seem to make sense but then don't, and while some of them are very meticulously calculated and rational, others are nuts by our standards. Besides, Auspex is one hell of a dru.. discipline, and put Necromancy on top of that, and damn, the things you can see man! One can make every case possible for this guy, and his Clan. I love Japphet as one of the most inconditional and even foolishly so fearless (not that he doesn't feel fear, but doesn't let it shake him) and compassionate Cainites in that time, because he clearly had all his trust in his father, but not blindly, and he accepted Claudius diablerie even if he didn't want it. So the Clan is full of gods, sinners, necromancers, saints and mercenaries. <br /> <br /> I personally think Cappadocius is insane, but like Captain Ahab, weaponized and galvanized his insanity, and even in a system that we don't know and can't understand, his plan makes sense. And that is a liberty any author can have when writing a thousands of years old vampire will unimaginable wisdom, powers and esoteric dealings. Also, he really was making himself the Lamb of God in this, like it has been said in this topic. By all the faults of GC part 1 (Last Supper), especially as a game, it does make a very tragic and dramatic religious play, from the first scene to the last. And I believe every form of Children of Isaac will probably hinder the Cappadocians without understanding what they are really doing and dealing with. Even those helping won't really understand, and only with time they might get bits of it. Like yeah, Giovanni, Hardestadt and Jappeth will all say different things, with the latter and his father being the most cryptic, with only being understood to a layman that &quot;he will try to eat god&quot;... which wouldn't sit well with nobody at that time I suppose.<br /> <br /> Thing is, I do believe in some point, during or after his diablerie, something went wrong, or not according to plan. Maybe it just took a lot of time off, maybe it had unthought consequences, but maybe it didn't stop his plan totally. But if Cappadocius's plan is still on, than I would like to know if Cappuchin would promote or be against it... <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:27:26-07:00","id":1482685,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is that Cappadocius's supposed conversion to Christianity and his diablerie by Augustus Giovanni was linked. This is a bit different from my original post on this thread in 2016 and reflects some growth in my ideas.<br /> <br /> I don't believe Cappadocius was ever an orthodox Christian. He most likely believed in an extremely heretical Gnostic version of Christianity (which may not even reflect one of the real world versions, but be based on his own ideas). He sacrificed himself in order to gain special spiritual knowledge that would have released a &quot;divine spark&quot; that already existed within him (and possibly everyone else according to Gnostic views), but trapped in flesh. In this theory, the destruction of his physical body was a necessary precondition for that divinity to be released and Cappadocius to ascend to godhood (in some form). Allowing Augustus to betray him may have been an attempt by Cappadocius to mirror Judas' betrayal of Jesus for important symbolic purposes.<br /> <br /> And if he was some kind of Gnostic Christian, he would have a very different view of what &quot;God&quot; meant. Union with the Monad would mean becoming more powerful and wise than the Demiurge. This might be translated as &quot;diablerizing God&quot; or &quot;becoming God&quot; by people unfamiliar with Gnostic religions - such as members of the Giovanni family who grew up in a culture dominated by orthodox Christianity.<br /> <br /> Although this sounds crazy to us, it would be within the tradition of actual Gnostic religions. Incredibly, it would also fit the idea that Augustus only absorbed the vitae of Cappadocious and not his soul. <br /> <br /> Cappadocious struck me as the kind of person who thought he was playing 4th dimensional chess when everyone else was playing checkers. It's entirely possible he disdained the Jyhad and came to the same conclusion as WOPR. in the movie WarGames - the only winning move was not to play. So he may have been trying to circumvent the need for the Jyhad entirely and define his own victory conditions.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this was the intent of the actual writers/developers. It's just my interpretation of what they gave us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T18:21:49-07:00","id":1482693,"title":"","content":"Both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25534_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25534\" data-vbnamecard=\"25534\">Banu_Saulot</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> posts offer great possibilities, much better than the simply &quot;he's just bat crazy&quot; approach. In any case, I wonder why he bothers to protect Marianna <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T18:50:06-07:00","id":1482702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482693#post1482693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25534_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25534\" data-vbnamecard=\"25534\">Banu_Saulot</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> posts offer great possibilities, much better than the simply &quot;he's just bat crazy&quot; approach. In any case, I wonder why he bothers to protect Marianna <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't read the entirety of the minutiae of the Giovanni Chronicles, I storytold the 1st part, and will the 2nd (of which I read closely only half), the other ones I've read it, but not with detail. So I'm not sure how Cappadocius protects her, but who knows, maybe he thinks she shouldn't suffer from the mistakes of her 'father', which might include him (Cappadocius). But... I don't really know... maybe because she was the only person who actually tried to prevent him from being destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T19:00:45-07:00","id":1482704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But... I don't really know... maybe because she was the only person who actually tried to prevent him from being destroyed. </div> </div> </div>That would make some sense, in fact I really like the idea of a particular character being protected by an Antediluvian, something similar happens with Lambach with the Tzimisce Antediluvian. In fact, not only Antediluvian, but even Methuselah, like the Inconnu, etc. It opens up the way for many interesting stories, Lair of The Hidden include some possible iterations of that happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T01:51:40-07:00","id":1482728,"title":"","content":"If Cappadocius did/does want to kill or diablerise god, it doesn't necessarily have to mean he's a self-absorbed monster drunk on power. Maybe after thousands of years watching death and rot and the Underworld getting worse and worse he decided the world is fundamentally an unjust mess and needs new management or something. This is the guy who has been noted to be obsessed with death and how and why it happens, maybe he wants a world that isn't warped and breaking down under the weight of all the death and suffering in it.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of the Capuchin's comment on the goal he's helping Augustus work towards is &quot;the heat death of the universe&quot; and the nothingness to follow, while the Hecata are talking about the world being in the decay stage of the cycle of existence and heading for a rebirth that they're guiding, or at least observing. I also get the impression that as of v5, the clan of death is getting cosier with the Followers of Set, indicating an interesting potential overlap of worldview and goals. If the clan is a reflection of its founder, Cappadocius doesn't seem enamoured of creation.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean it's a good plan, but his intentions might be benevolent or somewhere in the area thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-02-2022, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T04:46:17-07:00","id":1482731,"title":"","content":"I'd like to posit something: <br /> <br /> Augustus was the only person to successfully diablerize an Ante without hiccup or disclaimer. When Tremere ate Saulot, he entered Torpor, when Gratiano ate Lasombra, he refused the title of eldest and settled quietly in his little corner of the world. When Tzmisce was eaten... well, it's Tzmisce. But when August ate big Cappa, he announced it to the world, sat on a bigger chair, and solidified rule of his bloodline-come-clan: Huge success. <br /> <br /> This is a pretty threatening narrative. No no no, you can't just eat someone powerful and not get like, possessed, Torpored, or some other shit, that'll give the middling elders some very dangerous thoughts, and the effect on Ancilae and neonates will be even worse. This needed to be safely rationalized. <br /> And so, Capadocius was &quot;insane&quot; and allowed it to happen in his insanity. It was a one-off. You try that on a sane 3rd, 4th, 5th or even 6th gen like Montano or Toreador and they'll doubtlessly rule your body like it was theirs. Remember kids, not only is Diablerie badwrong-evil, it's fruitless and stupid and a good way to end your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T05:27:39-07:00","id":1482734,"title":"","content":"While obviously the Giovanni are objectively inherently superior and the best at vampirism like they've always told everyone, you could take that a step further. Every single founder either died or got eaten and those guys we think are the Antes are just the more recent inheritors of 3rd generation vitae. All vampire lore is lie upon lie to make the younger monsters hesitate before they try and eat you and nobody even remembers the truth anymore. The other part of the lie is &quot;Yes, I'm totally the millennia old dude who founded this clan inhabiting the body of the century old whelp who tried to kill me. I'm very scary Don't question me or try to eat my soul.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-02-2022, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T10:44:45-07:00","id":1482795,"title":"","content":"AFAIK Cappadocius was confirmed at first to be a Gnostic, or at least heavily hinted to be. That's already similar to the Setites, with the distinction that he wouldn't be of a &quot;Gnostic-based fictional faith&quot;, but an actual Gnostic (yes, with some idiosyncratic beliefs in the middle, but that's also pretty standard for Gnostics). But the &quot;Diablerize God&quot; part isn't stated as a metaphor in the books, and that's my problem.<br /> <br /> That, and given age and whatnot I really don't think that madness is unlikely. Actually I find it extremely ableist to assume that you can only be smart and effective if you're completely rational and mentally sound, specially when most &quot;normal&quot; people are already perfectly capable of acting on completely irrational beliefs.<br /> <br /> But I do think he may have succeeded at the basic Gnostic goal, it's just the goal to eat God that was unfeasible. He may be more powerful than ever by having transcended beyond Ialdabaoth, and it may even be that his Gnostic beliefs are mostly right and through that he reached the <i>Pleroma</i> and joined the Aeons above the very &quot;God&quot; that curse Caine.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to deny his Diablerie to be truth, either. Whatever spark is eaten during this action, it isn't necessarily the soul just because the <i>experience</i> of eating it seems like it. What's a soul for us to pinpoint when it is present or gone? Augustus' actions also have a powerful effect on the lore, and denying him that doesn't make for a better story. It reinforces the theme that Diablerie is a gamble, a mysterious action that won't have the same effects every time. He did it, be it by merit or dumb luck, and won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T11:18:07-07:00","id":1482802,"title":"","content":"That is for sure, Augustus won. Holy hell, his lineage size clan which was all family-based (even with some exceptions and flexing of the rule) usurped a really big and settled Clan in the middle of the Anarch Revolt, and even with the forming of the Camarilla (from which, the Founders wanted his hide) the Giovanni managed to thrive and parley. Their anathema status by the Founders didn't seem to affect them much, and I always assumed there were plenty of talks between Gios and Cams, that ended up in the Promise (not much long after the Convention of Thorns).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla just couldn't wage war against the Giovanni and the Sabbat simultaneously (as it couldn't against Anarchs and Haquimites and Giovanni). And one could say the clan of Augustus did really well, the best of wells, in comparison to the other independent Clans. From a merchant Italian family, to a worldwide Clan that deals almost shoulder-to-shoulder with the biggest sect, not bad, not bad at all. <br /> Something that always seemed weird for me was that if you had an Ante-eating usurper Clan, then it got ok. Like, it's like it gives the clan diplomatic immunity or something. I can reason why the Clans that diablerised 3rd gen vamps thrived, but, lightning struck twice at least. It makes me wonder what exactly dialberist did? What forms of power did they execute? How it made their Clan stronger, more concise and more legitimate? In a way I even imagine that most Clans would be even jealous, since their Founder are either dead or missing, and so are somewhat weakened or disparate (although you can't say that about the Ventrue or Banu Haqim). But it always made me wonder &quot;how did they get away with it&quot;, and if it was a lot of politicking or something more. <br /> <br /> <br /> And I also agree that... Antes are hardly what we could call mentally stable or sound. They are mostly geniuses, with baggage, sight and power to spare, even if they are alienated as all hell. I mean, who the hell has plans like the Eldest, Saulot and Cappdocius? of which we only hazard a guess most of the time. They seem to be completely focus, but at the same time lost in their Eternal Struggle, and path to Gehenna, waging their inner and outer Jyhad for millennia. <br /> There is also the fact that the metaplot and characters mostly live off the game, so diablerie is much more mysterious and weird, especially with Antes. Even though.... we never see a failed diablerie in the metaplot, although in-game you can very much fail. But that is another problem. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T09:11:00-07:00","id":1483040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten#post991397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As inspired by a recent trend where all the Diableries were, to borrow a phrase from another fictional universe &quot;just as planned&quot;. Tremere is Vampire Jesus, Tzitimze is Lugoj, Lasombra is in the Abyss, or something. But how does getting devoured (but apparently not fully, see the True Vessel) serve to push his plans forward?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't use modern day standards of sanity to ancient beings whom haven't been human for uncounted ages to figure them out. <br /> <br /> With Saulot allowing himself to be taken out by Tremere could be a means of buying time from topor and the methuslath thrist flaw to complete his schemes. Then we have Tzismce pulling a fast one on his clan by taking out and replacing his would be Brutus and tighting his grip on it's clan to achieve his goal of transendence.<br /> <br /> Cappadious maybe thought that having Augustus destroying his body would allow to move onto a higher plane of reality to replace God. It seems some of there plans worked on the notion of discarding there original forms. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T10:13:27-07:00","id":1483047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482802#post1482802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that always seemed weird for me was that if you had an Ante-eating usurper Clan, then it got ok. Like, it's like it gives the clan diplomatic immunity or something. I can reason why the Clans that diablerised 3rd gen vamps thrived, but, lightning struck twice at least. It makes me wonder what exactly dialberist did? What forms of power did they execute? How it made their Clan stronger, more concise and more legitimate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, the last documented and known (in the right circles of course) act of an Antediluvan was when Setite sorcerers led directly by the Antediluvian Set himself caused the volcano on the nearby island of Thera to erupt, burying Knossos beneath volcanic ash and obliterating Nergal's stronghold during the second Baali war in circa 1600 BC.<br /> (Cappadocious' Feast of Folly, the return of the Lasombra antediluvian in the early age of the Roman Republic, when he took residence in Sicily, building himself the tomb-fortress that would be called the Castle of Shadows by his descendants and the Embrace of Antonius and Erik Eigermann in Ancient Gaul by the mostly belived-to-be-dead Ventrue antediluvian before 60 BC wasn't so... noticable actually... and speaking of dead Antediluvians, Arikel, the Sculptor, whos heart was eaten by the Lasombra and settite Antediluivan according the ventrue, awoke from torpor around 260 BC and advised Prince Alchias of Syracuse.. or another Toreador Antediluvian, or at least Katherine of Montpelier insists that Ishtar is the Toreador Antediluvian, a bull-figher. Fought with the Gangrel Antediluvian and took shelter with King Minos, siring his son, who fell to the beast and became the 'Minotaur' of mythology.)<br /> That little stunt basically rewrote the geopolitical landscape not to mention a minor climate change that caused several long and harsh winters and very pale day time untill the ash settled<br /> An <b>active</b> Antediluvian - and an usurper is basically a young hothead with the power of a God - is bad news enough to give its ilk some... priviliges<br /> At least this is my two cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-04-2022, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T13:56:21-07:00","id":1483068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1483047#post1483047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, the last documented and known (in the right circles of course) act of an Antediluvan was when Setite sorcerers led directly by the Antediluvian Set himself caused the volcano on the nearby island of Thera to erupt, burying Knossos beneath volcanic ash and obliterating Nergal's stronghold during the second Baali war in circa 1600 BC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to point out that, the narrator of Clanbook: Baali, even more so than his counterparts in other clanbooks, is quite unreliable as a source of facts. For one <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Menele\" target=\"_blank\">Menele</a>, the Brujah methuselah that supposedly destroyed Pompeii millenia later with such a ritual, is cited as a participant, even though he would be embraced only 4 centuries later than Santorini's eruption.<br /> <br /> But speaking of Set's actions, there are also <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kemintiri\" target=\"_blank\">an event</a> of interest <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nefertiti\" target=\"_blank\">or two</a> that might be pointed out in later times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:05:29-07:00","id":1483071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1482731#post1482731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to posit something:<br /> Augustus was the only person to successfully diablerize an Ante without hiccup or disclaimer.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest?<br /> I'm not that sure<br /> He never Embraced after the &quot;succesfull&quot; diablerie of Cappadocius... there are no known 4th generation Giovanni (at least we don't now any)<br /> The only one is his son, Claudius Giovanni, who allegedly ate Japheth, but considering Japheth is now the Capuchin Trinity alongside Lazarus and Byzar, and he is a Wraith (thus the Diablerie was not completed, since major part is the consumption of the other's soul...) <br /> By this logic, Cappadocius, who ended up a wraith too &quot;survived&quot; his diableire, like Japheth...<br /> No soul consumption, no diablerie...<br /> Of course I could be wrong and the Generation hopping is tied to the potent blood (tho' according the Revised Dark Ages book Assamite studies of vitae have isolated the part within a vampire's blood that contains the soul. They call it &quot;heart's blood&quot; and it manifests as a thick, blackish liquid that quickly grows dry when it leaves the body, DAV20 goes a step further, and states, they have found a way to force the last drop of vitae within a vampire's body to calcify the heart into a semi-translucent grayish-white flask known as a &quot;Debitum&quot;. The Debitum enshrouds the spiritual essence (the &quot;heart's-blood&quot;) of the victim \u2013 which, if examined in detail, can be seen encased within, swimming in despair. Heart\u2019s-blood preserved in this way endures indefinitely. If vampiric fangs pierce it, the heart reanimates, pumping a cupful of celadon-colored, aqueous, non-burning flame vaguely resembling the victim into the vampire's maw. The vampire gains all the benefits of diablerie from this - Similar could have happened and the True Vessel contained the Heart's Blood of Cappadocius; no wonder he wanted it so badly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T14:10:31-07:00","id":1483072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1483068#post1483068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to point out that, the narrator of Clanbook: Baali, even more so than his counterparts in other clanbooks, is quite unreliable as a source of facts. For one <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Menele\" target=\"_blank\">Menele</a>, the Brujah methuselah that supposedly destroyed Pompeii millenia later with such a ritual, is cited as a participant, even though he would be embraced only 4 centuries later than Santorini's eruption.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except this is not from Clanbook Baali, but from the Dark Ages Companion, p. 171 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T15:47:43-07:00","id":1483079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/991397-why-did-cappadocious-allow-himself-to-be-eaten?p=1483072#post1483072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except this is not from Clanbook Baali, but from the Dark Ages Companion, p. 171 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is replicating from the former? Still doesn't change the issue of questionable reliability and continuity issues.<br /> But well, Dark Ages, take anyt bit of continuity or lore at face value at your own peril....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T12:14:39-07:00","id":1483632,"title":"","content":"A good reason to keep the antediluvians out of any story in general Shadowprowler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}